        contentEn: '<h1>Government intervenes in YPFB and announces restructuring after corruption complaints</h1><p><em>Hydrocarbons Minister Marcelo Blanco confirmed on Wednesday the intervention of the state oil company and the filing of criminal complaints over fuel diversion.</em></p><p>The Bolivian government announced the intervention of Yacimientos PetrolÃ­feros Fiscales Bolivianos (YPFB) to carry out a restructuring process after corruption complaints linked to fuel commercialization were detected. The decision was made under instructions from President Rodrigo Paz Pereira and includes internal investigations, asset audits and criminal complaints to be filed with the Public Prosecutor\'s Office.</p><p>"Where improper charges are verified, there will be immediate administrative sanctions and criminal complaints will be filed without delay, no matter who is involved," warned Minister Marcelo Blanco.</p><p><small>Source: Urgente.bo</small></p>',
