        contentEn: '<h1>Two Brazilian inmates escape from Palmasola after a blackout; three police officers arrested</h1><p><em>The inmates cut padlocks and climbed the wall with a rope during the early morning; one of them would be a PCC member.</em></p><p>The Bolivian Police confirmed the escape of two inmates of Brazilian nationality from Palmasola prison, the most populated in the country, located in Santa Cruz. The detainees took advantage of a power outage in the early hours of Wednesday to cut padlocks, climb the wall with a rope and flee the prison.</p><p>After the escape, the security forces activated "Plan Z" and deployed a massive search and recapture operation. According to reports, one of the fugitives would be a member of the First Capital Command (PCC).</p><p><small>Source: El Deber</small></p>',
