        contentEn: '<h1>Yungas coffee exported for $us 80,425 to South Korea</h1><p><em>The shipment of specialty green coffee departed for Seoul and represents the first Bolivian coffee consignment to an Asian market.</em></p><p>The Asipaem "El Mirador" ecological agroforestry producers\' association exported 9,600 kilos of specialty green coffee for $us 80,425 to South Korea, constituting the first foray of Bolivian Yungas coffee into the Asian market. The shipment is equivalent to half a container, made up of 316 sacks, and was purchased by On The Plan Coffee Company and Guapa Coffee of Seoul.</p><p>The coffee, of the Castillo variety grown at 1,600 meters above sea level, reached a cup score of 83 points and features notes of almond, walnut, honey, caramel, chamomile, peach, flaxseed and cocoa. The product has Fairtrade and EUDR certifications.</p><p><small>Source: El Mundo</small></p>',
