        titleEs: 'Evo Morales quiere volver a lanzarse en 2030: pidiÃ³ a sus seguidores activarse en campaÃ±a',
        titleEn: 'Evo Morales wants to run again in 2030: he asked his followers to start campaigning',
        excerptEs: 'El expresidente instruyÃ³ a sus seguidores "activarse" con la campaÃ±a desde ya, pese a que el TCP ha establecido que la reelecciÃ³n presidencial estÃ¡ limitada a dos periodos.',
        excerptEn: 'The former president told his followers to start campaigning right away, even though the TCP has established that presidential re-election is limited to two terms.',
        contentEs: `<h1>Evo Morales quiere volver a lanzarse en 2030: pidiÃ³ a sus seguidores activarse en campaÃ±a</h1><p><em>El expresidente de Bolivia revelÃ³ sus intenciones de volver a la presidencia en 2030 a pesar de la sentencia del Tribunal Constitucional Plurinacional que limita la reelecciÃ³n a dos periodos.</em></p><p>Evo Morales Ayma, lÃ­der del movimiento Evo Pueblo y expresidente de Bolivia, revelÃ³ sus intenciones de avanzar a la campaÃ±a presidencial del 2030. Morales instruyÃ³ a sus seguidores "activarse" con la campaÃ±a desde ya.</p><p>La iniciativa se produce cuando el gobierno de Rodrigo Paz cumple apenas nueve meses y a pesar de que el Tribunal Constitucional Plurinacional (TCP) ha establecido de forma reiterada que la reelecciÃ³n presidencial estÃ¡ limitada a un mÃ¡ximo de dos periodos, continuos o discontinuos.</p><h2>Congreso para "refundar el instrumento polÃ­tico"</h2><p>En la reuniÃ³n de dirigentes de Evo Pueblo realizada en el trÃ³pico de Cochabamba se resolviÃ³ elaborar una agenda polÃ­tica y convocar a un congreso nacional para "refundar el instrumento polÃ­tico", previsto para marzo de 2027.</p><p>El exdiputado evista Anyelo CÃ©spedes planteÃ³ la realizaciÃ³n de un referÃ©ndum nacional con una sola pregunta: "Â¿si estÃ¡ de acuerdo, sÃ­ o no, de que Evo Morales vuelva a ser candidato?", argumentando que de esta manera se evitarÃ­a cualquier interpretaciÃ³n o decisiÃ³n polÃ­tica que impida una eventual postulaciÃ³n.</p><h2>Un lÃ­mite constitucional</h2><p>Morales gobernÃ³ durante tres periodos (2006-2010, 2010-2015 y 2015-2019) y la Sentencia Constitucional Plurinacional 1010/2023, fundamentada en la opiniÃ³n consultiva OC-28/21 de la Corte Interamericana de Derechos Humanos, declarÃ³ que la reelecciÃ³n indefinida no es un derecho humano y limitÃ³ el ejercicio del cargo a un mÃ¡ximo de dos periodos, por lo que Morales quedÃ³ inhabilitado y en teorÃ­a no podrÃ­a volver a lanzarse.</p><p><small>Con informaciÃ³n de: <a href="https://www.bolivia.com/actualidad/nacionales/evo-morales-desafia-el-veto-del-tcp-y-ya-prepara-su-campana-para-el-2030-595589">Bolivia.com</a></small></p>`,
        contentEn: `<h1>Evo Morales wants to run again in 2030: he asked his followers to start campaigning</h1><p><em>Bolivia's former president revealed his intention to return to the presidency in 2030 despite the ruling by the Plurinational Constitutional Court that limits re-election to two terms.</em></p><p>Evo Morales Ayma, leader of the Evo Pueblo movement and former president of Bolivia, revealed his intention to move toward the 2030 presidential campaign. Morales instructed his followers to begin campaigning right away.</p><p>The initiative comes as Rodrigo Paz's government is barely nine months old and even though the Plurinational Constitutional Court (TCP) has repeatedly established that presidential re-election is limited to a maximum of two consecutive or non-consecutive terms.</p><h2>Congress to "refound the political instrument"</h2><p>At a meeting of Evo Pueblo leaders in the Chapare region of Cochabamba, it was decided to build a political agenda and call a national congress to "refound the political instrument", scheduled for March 2027.</p><p>Former evista deputy Anyelo CÃ©spedes proposed holding a national referendum with a single question: "Do you agree, yes or no, that Evo Morales should be a candidate again?", arguing that this would avoid any interpretation or political decision preventing a possible candidacy.</p><h2>A constitutional limit</h2><p>Morales governed for three terms (2006-2010, 2010-2015 and 2015-2019), and Plurinational Constitutional Court Ruling 1010/2023, based on Advisory Opinion OC-28/21 of the Inter-American Court of Human Rights, declared that indefinite re-election is not a human right and limited the exercise of the presidency to a maximum of two terms, leaving Morales ineligible and, in theory, unable to run again.</p><p><small>Source: <a href="https://www.bolivia.com/actualidad/nacionales/evo-morales-desafia-el-veto-del-tcp-y-ya-prepara-su-campana-para-el-2030-595589">Bolivia.com</a></small></p>`,
        date: '2026-08-11',
        readTimeEs: '5 min de lectura',
        readTimeEn: '4 min read',
        imageUrl: '/images/news/2026-08-13-evo-campana-2030.jpg',
        imageCaption: 'El expresidente Evo Morales en un acto con sus seguidores. Imagen: captura Twitter',
        categoryEs: 'PolÃ­tica',
        categoryEn: 'Politics',
        enableComments: true,
        featured: true,
        breaking: false,
        views: 1,
        location: 'TrÃ³pico de Cochabamba, Bolivia',
        source: 'BOLIVIA.COM',
