        titleEs: 'Un tribunal de Siria condena a muerte al dictador Bachar el Asad, exiliado en MoscÃº',
        titleEn: 'A Syrian court sentences dictator Bashar al-Assad to death in exile in Moscow',
        excerptEs: 'El tribunal lo declarÃ³ culpable de crÃ­menes de lesa humanidad en la primera sentencia en su contra desde la caÃ­da del rÃ©gimen en 2024.',
        excerptEn: 'The court found him guilty of crimes against humanity in the first sentence against him since the fall of the regime in 2024.',
        contentEs: `<h1>Un tribunal de Siria condena a muerte al dictador Bachar el Asad, exiliado en MoscÃº</h1><p><em>La corte encuentra culpable de crÃ­menes de lesa humanidad al exdirigente en la primera sentencia en su contra desde la caÃ­da del rÃ©gimen en 2024.</em></p><p>Un tribunal de Siria condenÃ³ a muerte en ausencia al expresidente Bashar el Asad, tras declararlo culpable de crÃ­menes de guerra y crÃ­menes de lesa humanidad cometidos durante los 14 aÃ±os de conflicto en el paÃ­s, que dejaron alrededor de medio millÃ³n de muertos.</p><p>La sentencia es la primera dictada en su contra bajo las autoridades de transiciÃ³n, que en 2026 comenzaron a juzgar a figuras del antiguo Gobierno, tanto de forma presencial como en ausencia.</p><h2>TambiÃ©n condenados otros altos cargos</h2><p>En el mismo proceso fue condenado a muerte Atef Najib, primo materno de Asad, por liderar la represiÃ³n en la provincia meridional de Daraa que desencadenÃ³ el levantamiento y posteriormente la guerra civil. Bajo fuertes medidas de seguridad, Najib permaneciÃ³ dentro de una jaula mientras el juez leÃ­a la sentencia.</p><p>El tribunal tambiÃ©n condenÃ³ en ausencia a varios antiguos altos cargos militares y de seguridad, entre ellos el hermano de Al Asad, Maher, y el exministro de Defensa Fahd al Freij, culpables de delitos que incluyen asesinato, tortura con resultado de muerte y privaciÃ³n reiterada de la libertad.</p><h2>Un juicio histÃ³rico</h2><p>Al Asad y su hermano huyeron a Rusia despuÃ©s de que los insurgentes entraran en Damasco en diciembre de 2024. El juicio en su contra habÃ­a comenzado en abril y se celebrÃ³ en su ausencia. Decenas de personas se reunieron frente al palacio de justicia portando fotos de sus seres queridos desaparecidos o encarcelados bajo el antiguo rÃ©gimen y expresaron su alegrÃ­a al conocer el veredicto.</p><p><small>Con informaciÃ³n de: <a href="https://elpais.com/internacional/2026-08-11/un-tribunal-de-siria-condena-en-rebeldia-al-dictador-bachar-el-asad-a-pena-de-muerte.html">El PaÃ­s</a> y <a href="https://www.france24.com/es/medio-oriente/20260811-tribunal-sirio-condena-a-muerte-en-ausencia-a-bashar-al-assad-por-cr%C3%ADmenes-de-lesa-humanidad">France 24</a></small></p>`,
        contentEn: `<h1>A Syrian court sentences dictator Bashar al-Assad to death in exile in Moscow</h1><p><em>The court found the former leader guilty of crimes against humanity in the first sentence against him since the fall of the regime in 2024.</em></p><p>A Syrian court sentenced former president Bashar al-Assad to death in absentia, after finding him guilty of war crimes and crimes against humanity committed during the country's 14-year conflict, which left around half a million people dead.</p><p>The sentence is the first issued against him under the transitional authorities, who in 2026 began to try figures from the former government, both in person and in absentia.</p><h2>Other senior officials also sentenced</h2><p>In the same trial, Atef Najib, Assad's maternal cousin, was sentenced to death for leading the repression in the southern province of Daraa that triggered the uprising and later the civil war. Under heavy security, Najib remained inside a cage while the judge read the sentence.</p><p>The court also sentenced in absentia several former senior military and security officials, including Assad's brother Maher and former defense minister Fahd al-Freij, guilty of offenses including murder, torture resulting in death and repeated deprivation of liberty.</p><h2>A historic trial</h2><p>Assad and his brother fled to Russia after insurgents entered Damascus in December 2024. The trial against him had begun in April and was held in his absence. Dozens of people gathered outside the court building carrying photos of their loved ones who had disappeared or been imprisoned under the former regime, expressing joy at the verdict.</p><p><small>Source: <a href="https://elpais.com/internacional/2026-08-11/un-tribunal-de-siria-condena-en-rebeldia-al-dictador-bachar-el-asad-a-pena-de-muerte.html">El PaÃ­s</a> and <a href="https://www.france24.com/es/medio-oriente/20260811-tribunal-sirio-condena-a-muerte-en-ausencia-a-bashar-al-assad-por-cr%C3%ADmenes-de-lesa-humanidad">France 24</a></small></p>`,
        date: '2026-08-11',
        readTimeEs: '5 min de lectura',
        readTimeEn: '4 min read',
        imageUrl: '/images/news/2026-08-13-asad-condenado.jpg',
        imageCaption: 'El expresidente sirio Bashar el Asad durante una entrevista televisiva en 2018. Imagen: El PaÃ­s',
        categoryEs: 'Internacional',
        categoryEn: 'International',
        enableComments: true,
        featured: true,
        breaking: true,
        views: 1,
        location: 'Damasco, Siria',
        source: 'EL PAÃS',
        region: 'International',
        sourceUrl: 'https://elpais.com/internacional/2026-08-11/un-tribunal-de-siria-condena-en-rebeldia-al-dictador-bachar-el-asad-a-pena-de-muerte.html'
