        titleEs: 'Rusia libera al exmarine estadounidense Robert Gilman, detenido desde 2022',
        titleEn: 'Russia releases former US Marine Robert Gilman, detained since 2022',
        excerptEs: 'Gilman fue liberado por razones humanitarias tras quedar en "condiciÃ³n que amenaza su vida" por un trato "duro y abusivo", segÃºn su familia.',
        excerptEn: 'Gilman was released on humanitarian grounds after being left in a "life-threatening condition" due to "harsh and abusive treatment", his family says.',
        contentEs: `<h1>Rusia libera al exmarine estadounidense Robert Gilman, detenido desde 2022</h1><p><em>Robert Gilman, quien fue arrestado en 2022, quedÃ³ en una "condiciÃ³n que amenaza su vida" tras ser sometido a un trato "duro y abusivo", segÃºn su familia.</em></p><p>Rusia liberÃ³ al exmarine estadounidense Robert Gilman, detenido desde 2022, quien partiÃ³ de vuelta a Estados Unidos para recibir atenciÃ³n mÃ©dica tras ser liberado por razones humanitarias.</p><p>La liberaciÃ³n fue confirmada por el presidente estadounidense Donald Trump, quien indicÃ³ que Rusia aceptÃ³ dejar en libertad a Gilman, de 32 aÃ±os, por motivos humanitarios despuÃ©s de conversaciones con el presidente ruso VladÃ­mir Putin.</p><h2>Un caso de salud crÃ­tica</h2><p>La familia de Gilman denunciÃ³ que fue sometido a "trato duro y abusivo" durante su detenciÃ³n y que quedÃ³ en una "condiciÃ³n que amenaza su vida". Organizaciones que representan a su familia relataron que fue trasladado en un estado similar al catatÃ³nico, diagnosticado como "estupor disociativo".</p><p>Gilman, quien servÃ­a en el Cuerpo de Marines, fue arrestado en enero de 2022 en Voronezh, acusado de agredir a un policÃ­a ruso mientras estaba alcoholizado, una versiÃ³n que sus familiares rechazan aduciendo que contrajo una enfermedad y golpeÃ³ al oficial de forma accidental.</p><h2>Una liberaciÃ³n sin canje</h2><p>Las autoridades de Estados Unidos seÃ±alaron que la liberaciÃ³n no implicÃ³ ningÃºn intercambio de prisioneros ni concesiones, y que Gilman fue evaluado por cuatro mÃ©dicos durante el vuelo de regreso, tras lo cual fue trasladado a un centro de rehabilitaciÃ³n en Texas.</p><p>La liberaciÃ³n de Gilman se produjo en medio de reportes sobre su delicado estado de salud que generaron presiÃ³n internacional para asegurar su retorno.</p><p><small>Con informaciÃ³n de: <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvgj4m8e1ryo">BBC News</a> y <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/russia-frees-ailing-ex-us-marine-robert-gilman-detention-2026-08-11/">Reuters</a></small></p>`,
        contentEn: `<h1>Russia releases former US Marine Robert Gilman, detained since 2022</h1><p><em>Robert Gilman, who was arrested in 2022, was left in a "life-threatening condition" after being subjected to "harsh and abusive treatment", his family says.</em></p><p>Russia released former US Marine Robert Gilman, detained since 2022, who departed back to the United States to receive medical care after being freed on humanitarian grounds.</p><p>The release was confirmed by US President Donald Trump, who said Russia agreed to free Gilman, 32, on humanitarian grounds after discussions with Russian President Vladimir Putin.</p><h2>A case of critical health</h2><p>Gilman's family denounced that he was subjected to "harsh and abusive treatment" during his detention and was left in a "life-threatening condition". Organizations representing his family recounted that he was transferred in a catatonic-like state, diagnosed as a "dissociative stupor".</p><p>Gilman, who served in the Marine Corps, was arrested in January 2022 in Voronezh, accused of assaulting a Russian police officer while intoxicated, a version his family rejects, saying he fell ill and accidentally kicked the officer.</p><h2>A release without exchange</h2><p>US authorities said the release involved no prisoner swap or concessions, and that Gilman was evaluated by four doctors during the return flight before being transferred to a rehabilitation center in Texas.</p><p>Gilman's release came amid reports about his delicate health that generated international pressure to secure his return.</p><p><small>Source: <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvgj4m8e1ryo">BBC News</a> and <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/russia-frees-ailing-ex-us-marine-robert-gilman-detention-2026-08-11/">Reuters</a></small></p>`,
        date: '2026-08-11',
