        slug: 'muerte-hayden-panettiere-autopsia-sin-trauma',
        titleEs: 'Muerte de Hayden Panettiere: la autopsia no hallÃ³ signos de trauma y se desconoce la causa',
        titleEn: 'Hayden Panettiere death: autopsy finds no signs of trauma, cause still unknown',
        excerptEs: 'La actriz de "Heroes" y "Nashville" fue hallada sin respuesta en un complejo de apartamentos de Greenville, Carolina del Sur. La autopsia descartÃ³ traumatismos, pero la causa y la manera de la muerte siguen en investigaciÃ³n.',
        excerptEn: 'The "Heroes" and "Nashville" actress was found unresponsive at a Greenville, South Carolina apartment complex. The autopsy ruled out trauma, but her cause and manner of death remain under investigation.',
        contentEs: '<h1>Muerte de Hayden Panettiere: la autopsia no hallÃ³ signos de trauma y se desconoce la causa</h1><p><em>La actriz Hayden Panettiere, conocida por sus papeles en "Heroes" y "Nashville", fue encontrada sin respuesta y luego declarada muerta el domingo en un complejo de apartamentos en Greenville, Carolina del Sur, segÃºn la PolicÃ­a. La autopsia, completada este lunes, no encontrÃ³ signos de trauma que contribuyan al deceso, pero la causa y la manera de la muerte siguen pendientes de investigaciÃ³n.</em></p><p>Los servicios de emergencia respondieron el domingo al mediodÃ­a a una llamada al 911 en el complejo Judson Mill Lofts, en Greenville, y localizaron a Panettiere, de 36 aÃ±os, en paro cardÃ­aco. SegÃºn la oficina del forense del condado de Greenville, los equipos "iniciaron medidas avanzadas de soporte vital cardÃ­aco", pero la reanimaciÃ³n no tuvo Ã©xito y la actriz fue declarada muerta a las 14:32 hora local. Un conocido suyo realizÃ³ la llamada al 911, segÃºn las autoridades.</p><h2>Autopsia y toxicologÃ­a</h2><p>La autopsia se completÃ³ este lunes y no revelÃ³ signos de traumatismo que hubieran contribuido a la muerte. La causa y el modo de deceso "permanecen pendientes de una mayor investigaciÃ³n y de la conclusiÃ³n de estudios adicionales". Los reportes iniciales no indican indicios de juego sucio ni circunstancias sospechosas, seÃ±alÃ³ la PolicÃ­a de Greenville.</p><h2>Una carrera desde la infancia</h2><p>Panettiere comenzÃ³ como actriz infantil y es recordada por sus papeles como Claire Bennet en la serie "Heroes" y como Juliette Barnes en el drama musical "Nashville". TambiÃ©n actuÃ³ en pelÃ­culas como "Remember the Titans", "Raising Helen", "Ice Princess" y "Scream 4". En mayo publicÃ³ sus memorias, "This Is Me: A Reckoning", en las que hablÃ³ de la depresiÃ³n posparto, la adicciÃ³n y la recuperaciÃ³n, entre otros temas.</p><h2>Reacciones</h2><p>Su padre, Skip Panettiere, pidiÃ³ privacidad "mientras nuestra familia procesa esta pÃ©rdida inimaginable". La actriz era madre de una hija, Kaya Klitschko, nacida en 2014 junto al ex boxeador Wladimir Klitschko. Su hermano, Jansen Panettiere, muriÃ³ en febrero de 2023 a los 28 aÃ±os. Panettiere habrÃ­a cumplido 37 aÃ±os el viernes.</p><p><small>Con informaciÃ³n de: <a href="https://abc7.com/post/details-911-call-released-hayden-panettieres-death/19692969/">ABC News</a></small></p>',
        contentEn: '<h1>Hayden Panettiere death: autopsy finds no signs of trauma, cause still unknown</h1><p><em>Actress Hayden Panettiere, best known for her roles in "Heroes" and "Nashville," was found unresponsive and later pronounced dead on Sunday at an apartment complex in Greenville, South Carolina, according to police. The autopsy, completed Monday, found no signs of trauma that would have contributed to her death, but her cause and manner of death remain under investigation.</em></p><p>Emergency responders arrived Sunday afternoon after a 911 call at the Judson Mill Lofts complex in Greenville and found Panettiere, 36, in cardiac arrest. First responders "initiated advanced cardiac life support measures," but resuscitation efforts were unsuccessful, and the actress was pronounced dead at 2:32 p.m. local time, according to the Greenville County Coroner\'s Office. An acquaintance of Panettiere placed the 911 call, authorities said.</p><h2>Autopsy and toxicology</h2><p>The autopsy was completed Monday and found no signs of trauma that would have contributed to her death. Her official cause and manner of death "remain pending further investigation and the completion of additional studies." Preliminary findings have not indicated any signs of foul play or suspicious circumstances, Greenville Police said.</p><h2>A career that began in childhood</h2><p>Starting as a child star, Panettiere is remembered as Claire Bennet on the hit series "Heroes" and as Juliette Barnes on the musical drama "Nashville." She also starred in "Remember the Titans," "Raising Helen," "Ice Princess" and "Scream 4." In May she released a memoir, "This Is Me: A Reckoning," opening up about postpartum depression, addiction and recovery, domestic abuse and loss.</p><h2>Reactions</h2><p>Her father, Skip Panettiere, asked for privacy "as our family takes time to process this unimaginable loss." The actress was the mother of a daughter, Kaya Klitschko, born in 2014 with former heavyweight champion Wladimir Klitschko. Her brother, Jansen Panettiere, died suddenly in February 2023 at age 28. Panettiere would have turned 37 on Friday.</p><p><small>Source: <a href="https://abc7.com/post/details-911-call-released-hayden-panettieres-death/19692969/">ABC News</a></small></p>',
        date: '2026-08-18',
        readTimeEs: '5 min de lectura',
        readTimeEn: '4 min read',
        imageUrl: '/images/blog/us-news/hayden-panettiere.jpg',
        imageCaption: 'Hayden Panettiere, en imagen de archivo. Foto: ABC News',
        categoryEs: 'EspectÃ¡culos',
        categoryEn: 'Entertainment',
        enableComments: true,
        featured: true,
        breaking: false,
        views: 1,
        location: 'Greenville, Carolina del Sur, EE.UU.',
