        contentType: 'news',
        slug: 'eeuu-sanciona-cpi-rubio-desmantelar',
        titleEs: 'EE.UU. sanciona al presidente y a un fiscal de la CPI y Rubio promete "desmantelar" la corte',
        titleEn: 'US sanctions ICC president and a prosecutor as Rubio vows to "dismantle" the court',
        excerptEs: 'El secretario de Estado Marco Rubio anunciÃ³ sanciones contra Tomoko Akane, presidenta de la Corte Penal Internacional, y el fiscal Abdoulaye Seye, que investigaba presuntos crÃ­menes de guerra de Israel en Gaza.',
        excerptEn: 'Secretary of State Marco Rubio announced sanctions on Tomoko Akane, president of the International Criminal Court, and prosecutor Abdoulaye Seye, who was investigating alleged Israeli war crimes in Gaza.',
        contentEs: '<h1>EE.UU. sanciona al presidente y a un fiscal de la CPI y Rubio promete "desmantelar" la corte</h1><p><em>Estados Unidos sancionÃ³ al presidente de la Corte Penal Internacional (CPI) y a un fiscal encargado de investigar presuntos crÃ­menes cometidos por Israel durante su guerra en Gaza, en un anuncio del secretario de Estado, Marco Rubio, que calificÃ³ a la corte de La Haya de "tribunal supranacional corrupto y fatalmente politizado".</em></p><p>Las designaciones anunciadas este martes apuntan contra la japonesa Tomoko Akane, presidenta de la CPI, y el senegalÃ©s Abdoulaye Seye, fiscal de la corte que investigaba los crÃ­menes israelÃ­es en Gaza. "Ha abusado maliciosamente de su autoridad y excedido su mandato", sostuvo Rubio en un comunicado.</p><h2>El acuerdo internacional</h2><p>La CPI, con sede en La Haya, es el Ãºnico tribunal internacional permanente para juzgar crÃ­menes de guerra, crÃ­menes de lesa humanidad y genocidio. Las sanciones coinciden con la investigaciÃ³n del tribunal sobre la conducta de Israel en el enclave palestino, que ha sido rechazada tanto por Israel como por Washington.</p><h2>La promesa de "desmantelar" la corte</h2><p>Las medidas se producen despuÃ©s de que Rubio prometiera "desmantelar" el tribunal internacional, como adelantÃ³ en una entrevista con CNN a mediados de julio. La Casa Blanca habÃ­a acusado previamente a la CPI de perseguir a Estados Unidos y a sus aliados.</p><p><small>Con informaciÃ³n de: <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/18/us-icc-sanctions">The Guardian</a></small></p>',
        contentEn: '<h1>US sanctions ICC president and a prosecutor as Rubio vows to "dismantle" the court</h1><p><em>The United States has sanctioned the president of the International Criminal Court (ICC) and a prosecutor tasked with investigating alleged crimes committed by Israel during its war on Gaza, in an announcement by Secretary of State Marco Rubio, who called the Hague-based court a "corrupt and fatally politicized supranational court."</em></p><p>The designations, announced on Tuesday, target Tomoko Akane of Japan, the ICC president, and Abdoulaye Seye of Senegal, an ICC prosecutor investigating Israeli crimes in Gaza. The court "has maliciously abused its authority and exceeded its mandate," Rubio said in a statement.</p><h2>The Hague court</h2><p>The ICC, based in The Hague, is the world\'s only permanent international tribunal for trying war crimes, crimes against humanity and genocide. The sanctions follow the court\'s investigation into Israel\'s conduct in the Palestinian enclave, which both Israel and Washington have rejected.</p><h2>Vow to "dismantle" the court</h2><p>The measures come after Rubio pledged to "dismantle" the tribunal, as he told CNN in mid-July. The White House had previously accused the ICC of targeting the United States and its allies.</p><p><small>Source: <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/18/us-icc-sanctions">The Guardian</a></small></p>',
        date: '2026-08-18',
        readTimeEs: '4 min de lectura',
        readTimeEn: '3 min read',
