    titleEs: `PakistÃ¡n: las inundaciones de monzÃ³n de 2026 superan las 159 vÃ­ctimas mortales`,
    titleEn: `Pakistan: 2026 monsoon floods surpass 159 deaths`,
    excerptEs: `El NDMA confirma al menos 159 fallecidos y mÃ¡s de 470 heridos por las lluvias desde finales de junio; la provincia de Khyber Pakhtunkhwa es la mÃ¡s golpeada.`,
    excerptEn: `The NDMA confirms at least 159 dead and over 470 injured from rains since late June; Khyber Pakhtunkhwa is the worst hit.`,
    contentEs: `<p class="lead"><em>Las lluvias monzÃ³nicas que azotan PakistÃ¡n desde finales de junio de 2026 han dejado al menos 159 personas fallecidas y mÃ¡s de 470 heridas, segÃºn el Ãºltimo balance de la Autoridad Nacional de GestiÃ³n de Desastres (NDMA) difundido el 17 de agosto.</em></p><figure class="report-figure"><img src="/images/blog/pakistan-inundaciones-monzon-2026-muertos-ndma.jpg" alt="Inundaciones por monzon en Sindh, Pakistan." loading="lazy"><figcaption>Inundaciones por monzon en Sindh, Pakistan.</figcaption></figure><p>La provincia de Khyber Pakhtunkhwa concentra la mayor parte de las vÃ­ctimas, con 55 muertos, seguida de Punjab, con 36, y Sindh. Las autoridades advierten que el nÃºmero podrÃ­a aumentar a medida que continÃºan las tormentas en el valle del Indo.</p><p>En las llanuras de Punjab, cerca de Lahore y Gujranwala, unas 400 kilÃ³metros cuadrados de cultivo y asentamientos permanecen bajo el agua, segÃºn reportes de la prensa local recogidos por <em>Dawn</em>. Miles de familias han sido desplazadas a refugios temporales.</p><div class="tweet-card"><div class="tweet-avatar" style="background:#117e3b">A</div><div class="tweet-body"><div class="tweet-name">Al Jazeera English <span class="tweet-verified" title="Cuenta verificada">&#10004;</span></div><div class="tweet-handle">@AJEnglish</div><p class="tweet-text">Pakistan's monsoon death toll passes 159 as floods submerge hundreds of square kilometres in Punjab. NDMA warns of more storms in the Indus valley.</p><div class="tweet-meta">25 ago 2026 &middot; <a href="https://x.com/AJEnglish" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ver en X &#8594;</a></div></div></div><p>El contexto es sombrÃ­o: en 2025, las inundaciones en el mismo paÃ­s causaron 1.037 muertes y afectaron a decenas de millones de personas, segÃºn cifras oficiales. Los expertos vinculan la creciente intensidad de los monzones con el cambio climÃ¡tico.</p><div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">159+</div><div class="stat-label">Fallecidos (NDMA, 17 ago)</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">470+</div><div class="stat-label">Heridos</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">55</div><div class="stat-label">Muertos en Khyber Pakhtunkhwa</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">~400 kmÂ²</div><div class="stat-label">Inundados en Punjab</div></div></div><p>El gobierno ha desplegado al ejÃ©rcito para tareas de rescate y distribuciÃ³n de ayuda, mientras organizaciones humanitarias solicitan fondos internacionales de emergencia.</p><p>Con informaciÃ³n de: NDMA, Al Jazeera y Dawn.</p>`,
    contentEn: `<p class="lead"><em>Monsoon rains battering Pakistan since late June 2026 have left at least 159 people dead and more than 470 injured, according to the latest National Disaster Management Authority (NDMA) tally released on 17 August.</em></p><figure class="report-figure"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1489599849927-2ee91cede3ba?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=70" alt="Monsoon rains in South Asia, 2026 (illustrative image)." loading="lazy"><figcaption>Monsoon rains in South Asia, 2026 (illustrative image).</figcaption></figure><p>Khyber Pakhtunkhwa province accounts for the largest share of victims with 55 dead, followed by Punjab with 36 and Sindh. Authorities warn the toll may rise as storms continue across the Indus valley.</p><p>In the Punjab plains near Lahore and Gujranwala, roughly 400 square kilometres of cropland and settlements remain underwater, according to local press reporting compiled by <em>Dawn</em>. Thousands of families have been moved to temporary shelters.</p><div class="tweet-card"><div class="tweet-avatar" style="background:#117e3b">A</div><div class="tweet-body"><div class="tweet-name">Al Jazeera English <span class="tweet-verified" title="Cuenta verificada">&#10004;</span></div><div class="tweet-handle">@AJEnglish</div><p class="tweet-text">Pakistan's monsoon death toll passes 159 as floods submerge hundreds of square kilometres in Punjab. NDMA warns of more storms in the Indus valley.</p><div class="tweet-meta">Aug 25 2026 &middot; <a href="https://x.com/AJEnglish" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ver en X &#8594;</a></div></div></div><p>The backdrop is grim: in 2025, floods in the same country killed 1,037 people and affected tens of millions, per official figures. Experts link the growing intensity of monsoons to climate change.</p><div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">159+</div><div class="stat-label">Dead (NDMA, Aug 17)</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">470+</div><div class="stat-label">Injured</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">55</div><div class="stat-label">Dead in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">~400 kmÂ²</div><div class="stat-label">Flooded in Punjab</div></div></div><p>The government has deployed the army for rescue and relief distribution as humanitarian groups appeal for international emergency funds.</p><p>With information from: NDMA, Al Jazeera and Dawn.</p>`,
    date: '2026-08-25',
    readTimeEs: '5 min',
    readTimeEn: '5 min',
    imageUrl: '/images/blog/pakistan-inundaciones-monzon-2026-muertos-ndma.jpg',
    imageCaption: 'Inundaciones por monzon en la provincia de Sindh, Pakistan. Fuente: Wikimedia Commons.',
