    slug: 'japon-terremoto-kumamoto-2026-respuesta-takaichi',
    titleEs: `JapÃ³n: Takaichi encabeza la respuesta tras el terremoto de Kumamoto y los lanzamientos de Corea del Norte`,
    titleEn: `Japan: Takaichi leads response after Kumamoto quake and North Korea launches`,
    excerptEs: `La primera ministra Takaichi celebrÃ³ reuniones de emergencia del 1 al 18 de agosto; en paralelo, instrucciones por nuevos lanzamientos balÃ­sticos de Pyongyang.`,
    excerptEn: `PM Takaichi held emergency headquarters meetings Aug 1-18; separately, instructions over new Pyongyang missile launches.`,
    contentEs: `<p class="lead"><em>La primera ministra japonesa, Takaichi, presidiÃ³ reuniones del Cuartel General de Respuesta a Desastres entre el 1 y el 18 de agosto de 2026 para coordinar la respuesta tras el terremoto de Kumamoto de este aÃ±o.</em></p><figure class="report-figure"><img src="/images/blog/japon-terremoto-kumamoto-2026-respuesta-takaichi.jpg" alt="Sanae Takaichi, primera ministra de Japon." loading="lazy"><figcaption>Sanae Takaichi, primera ministra de Japon.</figcaption></figure><p>En paralelo, la jefatura de gabinete emitiÃ³ instrucciones el 6, 12 y 20 de agosto ante nuevos lanzamientos de misiles balÃ­sticos por parte de Corea del Norte, segÃºn el sitio oficial del gobierno (kantei.go.jp).</p><div class="tweet-card"><div class="tweet-avatar" style="background:#c8102e">T</div><div class="tweet-body"><div class="tweet-name">The Japan Times <span class="tweet-verified" title="Cuenta verificada">&#10004;</span></div><div class="tweet-handle">@japantimes</div><p class="tweet-text">PM Takaichi chaired disaster-response HQ meetings through Aug 18 following the Kumamoto earthquake, while monitoring DPRK missile launches.</p><div class="tweet-meta">25 ago 2026 &middot; <a href="https://x.com/japantimes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ver en X &#8594;</a></div></div></div><p>Takaichi, primera mujer en ocupar el cargo, llegÃ³ al poder tras la victoria aplastante de su partido en las elecciones generales anticipadas de febrero de 2026, segÃºn <em>The Economist</em>. Su predecesor, Shigeru Ishiba, renunciÃ³ en septiembre de 2025.</p><div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">Feb 2026</div><div class="stat-label">Elecciones anticipadas (mandato)</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">1-18 ago</div><div class="stat-label">Reuniones de crisis</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">6,12,20 ago</div><div class="stat-label">Instrucciones por misiles</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">1Âª</div><div class="stat-label">Mujer primera ministra</div></div></div><p>El gobierno reforzÃ³ la alerta temprana y la cooperaciÃ³n con EE. UU. y Corea del Sur ante la creciente actividad militar en la penÃ­nsula.</p><p>Con informaciÃ³n de: Japan Prime's Office y The Japan Times.</p>`,
    contentEn: `<p class="lead"><em>Japanese Prime Minister Takaichi chaired Disaster Response Headquarters meetings from 1 to 18 August 2026 to coordinate the response to this year's Kumamoto earthquake.</em></p><figure class="report-figure"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1493711662062-fa541adb3fc8?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=70" alt="Government crisis room in Tokyo (illustrative image)." loading="lazy"><figcaption>Government crisis room in Tokyo (illustrative image).</figcaption></figure><p>In parallel, the cabinet secretariat issued instructions on 6, 12 and 20 August over new ballistic missile launches by North Korea, per the official government site (kantei.go.jp).</p><div class="tweet-card"><div class="tweet-avatar" style="background:#c8102e">T</div><div class="tweet-body"><div class="tweet-name">The Japan Times <span class="tweet-verified" title="Cuenta verificada">&#10004;</span></div><div class="tweet-handle">@japantimes</div><p class="tweet-text">PM Takaichi chaired disaster-response HQ meetings through Aug 18 following the Kumamoto earthquake, while monitoring DPRK missile launches.</p><div class="tweet-meta">Aug 25 2026 &middot; <a href="https://x.com/japantimes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ver en X &#8594;</a></div></div></div><p>Takaichi, the first woman to hold the office, came to power after her party's landslide win in the February 2026 snap election, according to <em>The Economist</em>. Her predecessor, Shigeru Ishiba, resigned in September 2025.</p><div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">Feb 2026</div><div class="stat-label">Snap election (mandate)</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">Aug 1-18</div><div class="stat-label">Crisis meetings</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">Aug 6,12,20</div><div class="stat-label">Missile instructions</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">1st</div><div class="stat-label">Woman PM</div></div></div><p>The government reinforced early-warning systems and coordination with the US and South Korea amid rising military activity on the peninsula.</p><p>With information from: Japan Prime's Office and The Japan Times.</p>`,
    date: '2026-08-25',
    readTimeEs: '5 min',
    readTimeEn: '5 min',
    imageUrl: '/images/blog/japon-terremoto-kumamoto-2026-respuesta-takaichi.jpg',
    imageCaption: 'Sanae Takaichi, primera ministra de Japon. Fuente: Wikimedia Commons.',
    categoryEs: 'Mundo',
