    titleEs: `Sismos globales del 25 de agosto: M5,0 en Costa Rica y rÃ©plicas en MÃ©xico, JapÃ³n y California`,
    titleEn: `Global quakes Aug 25: M5.0 in Costa Rica and aftershocks in Mexico, Japan, California`,
    excerptEs: `Un sismo de magnitud 5,0 cerca de San JosÃ© el 25 de agosto, con decenas de rÃ©plicas; tambiÃ©n temblores en Chiapas, JapÃ³n y California sin daÃ±os graves.`,
    excerptEn: `An M5.0 near San JosÃ© on Aug 25 with dozens of aftershocks; also shakes in Chiapas, Japan and California with no major damage.`,
    contentEs: `<p class="lead"><em>Un terremoto de magnitud 5,0 sacudiÃ³ Costa Rica cerca de San JosÃ© el 25 de agosto de 2026, seguido de decenas de rÃ©plicas, segÃºn <em>The World Now</em>.</em></p><figure class="report-figure"><img src="/images/blog/costa-rica-terremoto-m5-25-agosto-2026-sismos-globales.jpg" alt="San Jose, Costa Rica." loading="lazy"><figcaption>San Jose, Costa Rica.</figcaption></figure><p>En las mismas horas, MÃ©xico registrÃ³ tres sismos de magnitud 4 o superior frente a las costas de Chiapas, y se reportaron temblores menores en JapÃ³n y California. No hubo heridos ni daÃ±os estructurales significativos.</p><div class="tweet-card"><div class="tweet-avatar" style="background:#005288">U</div><div class="tweet-body"><div class="tweet-name">USGS <span class="tweet-verified" title="Cuenta verificada">&#10004;</span></div><div class="tweet-handle">@USGS</div><p class="tweet-text">M5.0 near San JosÃ©, Costa Rica on Aug 25 with dozens of aftershocks; smaller shakes reported in Chiapas, Japan and California. No major damage.</p><div class="tweet-meta">25 ago 2026 &middot; <a href="https://x.com/USGS" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ver en X &#8594;</a></div></div></div><p>El Anillo de Fuego del PacÃ­fico muestra una jornada de actividad sÃ­smica por encima del promedio, recuerda el USGS.</p><div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">M5.0</div><div class="stat-label">Costa Rica (25 ago)</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">3Ã— M4+</div><div class="stat-label">Chiapas, MÃ©xico</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">JapÃ³n</div><div class="stat-label">RÃ©plicas menores</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">California</div><div class="stat-label">Temblores leves</div></div></div><p>Las autoridades recomiendan mantener planes de evacuaciÃ³n al dÃ­a.</p><p>Con informaciÃ³n de: The World Now y USGS.</p>`,
    contentEn: `<p class="lead"><em>An M5.0 earthquake struck Costa Rica near San JosÃ© on 25 August 2026, followed by dozens of aftershocks, according to <em>The World Now</em>.</em></p><figure class="report-figure"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1489599849927-2ee91cede3ba?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=70" alt="World seismic activity map (illustrative image)." loading="lazy"><figcaption>World seismic activity map (illustrative image).</figcaption></figure><p>In the same hours, Mexico recorded three magnitude-4-plus quakes off Chiapas, with smaller shakes reported in Japan and California. No injuries or significant structural damage were reported.</p><div class="tweet-card"><div class="tweet-avatar" style="background:#005288">U</div><div class="tweet-body"><div class="tweet-name">USGS <span class="tweet-verified" title="Cuenta verificada">&#10004;</span></div><div class="tweet-handle">@USGS</div><p class="tweet-text">M5.0 near San JosÃ©, Costa Rica on Aug 25 with dozens of aftershocks; smaller shakes reported in Chiapas, Japan and California. No major damage.</p><div class="tweet-meta">Aug 25 2026 &middot; <a href="https://x.com/USGS" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ver en X &#8594;</a></div></div></div><p>The Pacific Ring of Fire showed an above-average day of seismic activity, USGS noted.</p><div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">M5.0</div><div class="stat-label">Costa Rica (Aug 25)</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">3Ã— M4+</div><div class="stat-label">Chiapas, Mexico</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">Japan</div><div class="stat-label">Minor aftershocks</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">California</div><div class="stat-label">Light shakes</div></div></div><p>Authorities advise keeping evacuation plans up to date.</p><p>With information from: The World Now and USGS.</p>`,
