    excerptEn: `An Aug 22 interview warns the conflict between Israel and NATO ally Turkey could spiral out of control.`,
    contentEs: `<p class="lead"><em>Las tensiones entre Israel y TurquÃ­a â€”aliada de la OTANâ€” crecen y podrÃ­an estallar en una guerra abierta, segÃºn advirtiÃ³ el exfuncionario estadounidense Chas Freeman en una entrevista del 22 de agosto difundida por el <em>Middle East Policy Council</em>.</em></p><figure class="report-figure"><img src="/images/blog/israel-turquia-tensiones-conflicto-2026.jpg" alt="Recep Tayyip Erdogan, presidente de Turquia." loading="lazy"><figcaption>Recep Tayyip Erdogan, presidente de Turquia.</figcaption></figure><p>La ruptura diplomÃ¡tica se agudiza por disputas regionales y la postura turca frente al conflicto en Gaza, reporta AFP.</p><div class="tweet-card"><div class="tweet-avatar" style="background:#bb1919">B</div><div class="tweet-body"><div class="tweet-name">BBC World <span class="tweet-verified" title="Cuenta verificada">&#10004;</span></div><div class="tweet-handle">@BBCWorld</div><p class="tweet-text">Analyst Chas Freeman warns the Israel-Turkey conflict could explode into open war, raising NATO entanglement risks in the Middle East.</p><div class="tweet-meta">25 ago 2026 &middot; <a href="https://x.com/BBCWorld" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ver en X &#8594;</a></div></div></div><p>La posibilidad de que un estado miembro de la OTAN se vea arrastrado a un conflicto regional preocupa a las cancillerÃ­as europeas.</p><div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">22 ago 2026</div><div class="stat-label">Advertencia de Freeman</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">OTAN</div><div class="stat-label">TurquÃ­a es miembro</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">Gaza</div><div class="stat-label">Eje de la disputa</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">AFP</div><div class="stat-label">Reporte diplomÃ¡tico</div></div></div><p>Los canales de comunicaciÃ³n de defensa permanecen activos para evitar una escalada.</p><p>Con informaciÃ³n de: Middle East Policy Council y AFP.</p>`,
    contentEn: `<p class="lead"><em>Tensions between Israel and Turkey â€” a NATO ally â€” are growing and could explode into open war, former US official Chas Freeman warned in an interview on 22 August carried by the <em>Middle East Policy Council</em>.</em></p><figure class="report-figure"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1493711662062-fa541adb3fc8?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=70" alt="Middle East, tension zone (illustrative image)." loading="lazy"><figcaption>Middle East, tension zone (illustrative image).</figcaption></figure><p>The diplomatic rupture deepens over regional disputes and Turkey's stance on the Gaza conflict, AFP reports.</p><div class="tweet-card"><div class="tweet-avatar" style="background:#bb1919">B</div><div class="tweet-body"><div class="tweet-name">BBC World <span class="tweet-verified" title="Cuenta verificada">&#10004;</span></div><div class="tweet-handle">@BBCWorld</div><p class="tweet-text">Analyst Chas Freeman warns the Israel-Turkey conflict could explode into open war, raising NATO entanglement risks in the Middle East.</p><div class="tweet-meta">Aug 25 2026 &middot; <a href="https://x.com/BBCWorld" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ver en X &#8594;</a></div></div></div><p>The prospect of a NATO member being drawn into a regional conflict worries European chancelleries.</p><div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">Aug 22 2026</div><div class="stat-label">Freeman warning</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">NATO</div><div class="stat-label">Turkey is a member</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">Gaza</div><div class="stat-label">Core dispute</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">AFP</div><div class="stat-label">Diplomatic report</div></div></div><p>Defence communication channels remain active to avoid escalation.</p><p>With information from: Middle East Policy Council and AFP.</p>`,
