    titleEs: `Yemen: ataques Houthi dejan 58 muertos y se firma un pacto militar saudÃ­-turco-paquistanÃ­`,
    titleEn: `Yemen: Houthi attacks kill 58 as Saudi-Turkey-Pakistan military pact signed`,
    excerptEs: `El 7 de agosto, misiles Houthi mataron a 58 yemenÃ­es respaldados por Riad; ese mismo dÃ­a se firmÃ³ un acuerdo militar entre Arabia Saudita, TurquÃ­a y PakistÃ¡n.`,
    excerptEn: `On Aug 7, Houthi missiles killed 58 Saudi-backed Yemenis; the same day a Saudi-Turkey-Pakistan military agreement was signed.`,
    contentEs: `<p class="lead"><em>Ataques con misiles de los Houthi causaron 58 muertos entre yemenÃ­es respaldados por Arabia Saudita el 7 de agosto de 2026, segÃºn AFP.</em></p><figure class="report-figure"><img src="/images/blog/yemen-houthi-58-muertos-pacto-saudi-turquia-pakistan.jpg" alt="Ciudad Vieja de Sana'a, Yemen." loading="lazy"><figcaption>Ciudad Vieja de Sana'a, Yemen.</figcaption></figure><p>Ese mismo dÃ­a, Arabia Saudita, TurquÃ­a y PakistÃ¡n firmaron un acuerdo de cooperaciÃ³n militar conjunta, reconfigurando los equilibrios de poder en la regiÃ³n.</p><div class="tweet-card"><div class="tweet-avatar" style="background:#117e3b">A</div><div class="tweet-body"><div class="tweet-name">Al Jazeera <span class="tweet-verified" title="Cuenta verificada">&#10004;</span></div><div class="tweet-handle">@AJEnglish</div><p class="tweet-text">Yemen: Houthi missile attacks killed 58 Saudi-backed Yemenis on Aug 7, as Riyadh, Turkey and Pakistan signed a joint military pact.</p><div class="tweet-meta">25 ago 2026 &middot; <a href="https://x.com/AJEnglish" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ver en X &#8594;</a></div></div></div><p>El pacto tripartito se interpreta como un contrapeso ante la inestabilidad en el sur de la penÃ­nsula arÃ¡biga.</p><div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">58</div><div class="stat-label">Muertos (7 ago)</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">7 ago 2026</div><div class="stat-label">Ataque e pacto</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">3 paÃ­ses</div><div class="stat-label">Saudi-TurquÃ­a-PakistÃ¡n</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">AFP</div><div class="stat-label">Fuente</div></div></div><p>La ONU renovÃ³ su llamado a un alto el fuego negociado.</p><p>Con informaciÃ³n de: AFP.</p>`,
    contentEn: `<p class="lead"><em>Houthi missile attacks killed 58 Saudi-backed Yemenis on 7 August 2026, according to AFP.</em></p><figure class="report-figure"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1493711662062-fa541adb3fc8?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=70" alt="Yemen conflict scene (illustrative image)." loading="lazy"><figcaption>Yemen conflict scene (illustrative image).</figcaption></figure><p>On the same day, Saudi Arabia, Turkey and Pakistan signed a joint military cooperation agreement, reshaping the regional balance of power.</p><div class="tweet-card"><div class="tweet-avatar" style="background:#117e3b">A</div><div class="tweet-body"><div class="tweet-name">Al Jazeera <span class="tweet-verified" title="Cuenta verificada">&#10004;</span></div><div class="tweet-handle">@AJEnglish</div><p class="tweet-text">Yemen: Houthi missile attacks killed 58 Saudi-backed Yemenis on Aug 7, as Riyadh, Turkey and Pakistan signed a joint military pact.</p><div class="tweet-meta">Aug 25 2026 &middot; <a href="https://x.com/AJEnglish" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ver en X &#8594;</a></div></div></div><p>The tripartite pact is read as a counterweight to instability in the southern Arabian peninsula.</p><div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">58</div><div class="stat-label">Dead (Aug 7)</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">Aug 7 2026</div><div class="stat-label">Attack & pact</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">3 states</div><div class="stat-label">Saudi-Turkey-Pakistan</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-value">AFP</div><div class="stat-label">Source</div></div></div><p>The UN renewed its call for a negotiated ceasefire.</p><p>With information from: AFP.</p>`,
